{"overview":{"Symbol":"KLRA","Name":"Kailera Therapeutics, Inc.","Description":"Kailera Therapeutics, Inc. operates as a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company developing therapies for obesity and related conditions. The company develops clinical- and preclinical-stage therapies, with a product pipeline that includes injectable peptides, oral peptides, and oral small molecules. Key programs include KAI-9531, an injectable GLP-1/GIP receptor dual agonist; KAI-7535, an oral small molecule GLP-1 receptor agonist; and KAI-4729, an injectable GLP-1/GIP/glucagon receptor tri-agonist. Kailera Therapeutics holds exclusive rights for global development and commercialization of four metabolic disease assets outside of Greater China, with therapies delivered through oral and injectable formulations. The company was founded in 2024 and is based in Waltham, Massachusetts.","CIK":"","Exchange":"NasdaqGS","Currency":"USD","Country":"United States","Sector":"Healthcare","Industry":"Biotechnology","Address":"180 Third Avenue, Waltham, MA, 02451, United States","FiscalYearEnd":"","LatestQuarter":"","MarketCapitalization":"2557625088","EBITDA":"-158030000","PERatio":"","PEGRatio":"","BookValue":"-18713.672","DividendPerShare":"","DividendYield":"","EPS":"-1.78","RevenuePerShareTTM":"","ProfitMargin":"0","OperatingMarginTTM":"0","ReturnOnAssetsTTM":"-0.22731","ReturnOnEquityTTM":"-0.36896","RevenueTTM":"","GrossProfitTTM":"","DilutedEPSTTM":"-1.78","QuarterlyEarningsGrowthYOY":"","QuarterlyRevenueGrowthYOY":"","AnalystTargetPrice":"42.6","TrailingPE":"","ForwardPE":"-5.291133","PriceToSalesRatioTTM":"","PriceToBookRatio":"","EVToRevenue":"","EVToEBITDA":"","Beta":"","52WeekHigh":"28.23","52WeekLow":"18.85","50DayMovingAverage":"22.490263","200DayMovingAverage":"22.490263","SharesOutstanding":"129565608","DividendDate":"","ExDividendDate":"","DebtToEquity":""},"daily":{"Meta Data":{"1. Information":"Daily Time Series (Yahoo Finance, shaped like Alpha Vantage)","2. Symbol":"KLRA","3. L